From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: eeprom: add BL24SA64 and GT24P64E

Describe the 64-Kbit Belling BL24SA64 and Giantec GT24P64E with the
existing AT24C64 fallback. The existing at24 driver supplies the 8-Kbyte,
16-bit address protocol; no vendor camera ioctl or new driver is needed.

Giantec identifies GT24P64E as a 64-Kbit part. Coreboot's pinned telith
GT24P64E declaration uses atmel,24c64, size 0x2000, width 0x10 and
readonly.
Belling's BL24SA64 V1.08 datasheet specifies the same memory organization
and two-byte random-read address. This does not select a board supplier,
slave address, calibration layout or permission to program either part.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/eeprom/at24.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/eeprom/at24.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/eeprom/at24.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/eeprom/at24.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/eeprom/at24.yaml
@@ -133,7 +133,9 @@ properties:
           - const: atmel,24c32
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - belling,bl24sa64
               - belling,bl24s64
               - giantec,gt24p64a
+              - giantec,gt24p64e
               - onnn,n24s64b
               - puya,p24c64f
